NeoSim
======

This repository is a derivative work of UniVTAC:

    UniVTAC: A Unified Simulation Platform for Visuo-Tactile Manipulation
    Data Generation, Learning, and Benchmarking
    Chen et al., arXiv:2602.10093
    https://github.com/byml-c/UniVTAC

used and modified under the MIT License. NeoSim is likewise distributed
under the MIT License (see LICENSE), and preserves the attribution the
license requires.

Modifications and extensions by the NeoSim authors (2026) include, among
others:
  - A new visuo-tactile representation (`gel_particle`) and force-field
    tooling (docs/TactileRepresentations.md)
  - Twelve additional manipulation tasks beyond upstream's nine: four
    single-arm (insert_USB, grasp_chip, pour_ball, phone_socket_replug)
    and eight dual-arm (envs/dual_*.py), together with their procedurally
    generated assets (scripts/asset_tools/), configs, and scripted experts
  - Revised and audited evaluation success criteria across tasks
    (e.g. insertion depth thresholds, stack/unstack alignment criteria;
    see docs/Tasks.md)
  - Policy-server evaluation clients (eval/) for VTA-style policies and
    multiple baselines, plus additional task/eval configurations
    (task_config/)

Vendored third-party software:

  third_party/TacEx
    TacEx — Tactile Extension for Isaac Sim/Isaac Lab (modified copy)
    https://github.com/DH-Ng/TacEx
    The upstream repository declares the MIT License in its README badge
    but does not ship a LICENSE file (as of 2026-07). This vendored,
    modified copy is redistributed following upstream's declared MIT
    intent and the precedent set by UniVTAC's public release; contact
    the TacEx authors for clarification before wider redistribution.

NeoSim also depends on NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab, cuRobo, and other
dependencies under their respective licenses.
